+bootmenu_1=UEFI Maintenance Menu=eficonfig
+/*
+ * Named TFTP boot entry for chainloading iPXE's SNP build (snp-arm64.efi).
+ * The UEFI boot manager cannot express a TFTP Boot#### option - its network
+ * loader is http:// only (wget) - so this is a plain U-Boot boot command:
+ * DHCP for an address, TFTP snp-arm64.efi from the DHCP next-server, then run
+ * it as an EFI application. U-Boot exposes the EFI Simple Network Protocol
+ * (efi_net, built with NETDEVICES) to the loaded image, so iPXE-snp gets a
+ * working NIC. Invoke with 'run boot_snp'; set bootcmd or once.env to
